{
  "summary": "repository_explore is a read-only AgentTool (src/agent_harness/integrations/repository_explorer.py) whose five focus arguments have very different, deliberately asymmetric roles. identifiers are case-sensitive exact code symbols: they are matched only against definition tags and, on a match, outrank everything (fixed +1000 per candidate score) and re-weight the graph edges (x10); if identifiers are supplied and none match any definition, the tool does not fail, it degrades to a filename-hint fallback over at most 12 files rendered as unexpanded file candidates with an explicit 'no symbol-level match is claimed' disclaimer. query is the conceptual entry point and is the only argument that can create a hard file filter: when query is present without identifiers, files whose path or symbol names do not contain any query term are dropped, definitions whose names contain a term are rendered (+30) and references to those seed definitions are surfaced as 'related implementation' (+25). focus_paths and known_paths are not filters but personalization signals (PageRank prior +50 / +10, candidate bonus +100) plus a post-ranking exclusion for known_paths; path_prefixes is a pure +10 boost that can never cut discovery (an identifier hit outside the prefix is still rendered). Ranking and rendering are two separate, deterministic orders: candidates are selected/truncated in score order (-score, path, line, name), then re-sorted into (path, line, name) order so the emitted map is always grouped per file alphabetically, independent of relevance. Freshness is handled at both stages: the index cache is keyed by (path, size, mtime_ns, INDEXER_VERSION, QUERY_VERSION) and every cache error is a miss, while each rendered snippet is verified by reading the file twice and comparing sha256/size/mtime_ns; a mismatch raises WorkspaceChangedDuringRender, which execute() retries exactly once against a fresh index, and a second failure becomes a bounded is_error result 'workspace_changed_during_render' instead of a corrupt snippet.",
