    "tool": "RepositoryExplorerTool (name 'repository_explore', replay_policy 'safe', terminate never set), registered only when settings.tools contains 'repository_explore' and repository_index_dir is set (src/agent_harness/api/serve.py::_repository_explorer)"
  },
  "flow": [
    "1. execute(arguments) -> _normalize_request: unknown keys, array sizes/byte caps, path existence/containment, known/focus disjointness, query length, max_tokens range, at-least-one-focus. Failures -> _bounded_error('repository_explore invalid arguments: ...').",
    "2. Index (asyncio.to_thread inside an asyncio.Semaphore(max_concurrent_indexes, default 2)): _discover walks the workspace with containment checks and skip-dirs, applies include_tests via _is_test_path, enforces file/size/time limits; per file a cache lookup by (path,size,mtime_ns,indexer_version,query_version) may return the tags, otherwise bytes are hashed, NUL-containing files become parseable=False with no tags, else tree-sitter tags are extracted and cached.",
    "3. Identifier matching: definitions = all tags with role 'definition'; matched_identifiers = supplied identifiers that equal some definition tag name exactly (case-sensitive).",
    "4. Branch: if identifiers were supplied and nothing matched -> _fallback_candidates (query words + words extracted from the identifiers become path-substring hints; scores: +100 per path term, +100 focus, +10 prefix, +5 ROOT_IMPORTANT_FILES, +5 .github/workflows, +1 for tagged files; top 12). Otherwise _rank_candidates; _rank_candidates itself falls back to _fallback_candidates when it produced no candidate at all.",
    "5. _rank_candidates: builds reference->definition edges weighted by sqrt(repetitions) x modifiers (identifier x10, compound name x10, leading underscore x0.1, >5 definitions x0.1, known referencer x50, low_confidence x0.1); if there are no edges at all it synthesizes co-definition edges (1.0) and self-loops (0.1) for dangling definition files; PageRank (damping 0.85, 30 iterations, personalization 1.0 +50 focus +10 known); candidate score = rank + 1000 (identifier definition) + 100 (focus) + 10 (path prefix) - 1 (test path) + _symbol_score_bonus + 30 (query-matched definition) / 25 (query-seed reference); query-only mode additionally drops files outside query_only_paths, renders only query-matched definitions and reference sites of query seed names; focus files that have no rendered symbol are appended as tag-less candidates at 100.0; duplicates (path,line,name,role) collapse to the higher-priority symbol kind; final sort key (-score, path, line, name).",
    "6. known_paths removal: after ranking, all candidates whose relative_path is in known_paths are filtered out (they still shaped the ranking as personalization/edge multipliers).",
    "7. Prefix lines: '# Repository exploration (<revision from .git/HEAD, else worktree>)', the verify-with-read reminder, then optionally 'identifiers_not_found: ...' and, only when nothing matched, 'Using unmatched identifiers only as filename hints; no symbol-level match is claimed.', then 'No matching symbols or eligible files were found.' when empty.",
    "8. Selection: iterate candidates in rank order; skip further tags of a file after MAX_SYMBOLS_PER_FILE=3 tag blocks; build each block (missing file or _safe_path failure -> WorkspaceChangedDuringRender); accept only while the *incremental* wire budget holds (50 KiB, 1600 lines, ceil(bytes/3) <= max_tokens) else stop with truncated=True.",
    "9. Re-order and group: selected.sort(key=_render_order) -> (path, line, name[, tag None => line 0]) so output is path-alphabetical and file-grouped regardless of score; a truncation note listing up to 12 omitted candidates is appended, and trailing selected blocks are popped (in that same sorted order) until the note fits, else the note itself is dropped and truncated stays True; _group_rendered_candidates merges adjacent same-path blocks into one '## `path`' section with 'snapshot `hash12`' and '### [`reference `]name` line N' subheads.",
    "10. Final guard: _within_wire_budget over the complete JSON payload; if the small prefix itself still overflows (pathological long identifiers), _trim_to_wire_budget binary-searches a prefix that fits and appends '\\n[truncated]'.",
    "11. Per-snippet freshness: _candidate_block reads the file, hashes it, reads it again and compares sha256 + st_size + st_mtime_ns; any difference (or a vanished/non-file target) raises WorkspaceChangedDuringRender. execute() retries the whole index+render cycle once (for attempt in range(2)); on the second failure the RepositoryIndexError handler returns is_error with content 'workspace_changed_during_render'. OSError -> 'repository_explore could not read workspace'; everything is clipped by _bounded_error (min(4000, 25 KiB)).",
    "12. Result: ToolExecutionResult(content=<markdown map>, is_error=False, details={'truncated': bool, 'token_estimate': True}) - truncation is reported in details plus the trailing note, not as an error, and the tool never sets terminate so it can never end the operation."
